      "worked": "Both $\\sec\\theta$ and $\\tan\\theta$ require $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$, so $90^{\\circ}$ and $270^{\\circ}$ are excluded.\n\nUsing $\\sec^2\\theta=1+\\tan^2\\theta$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sec^2\\theta-\\tan\\theta-1&=\\tan^2\\theta-\\tan\\theta\\\\\\sec^2\\theta-\\tan\\theta-1&=\\tan\\theta(\\tan\\theta-1)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\tan\\theta(\\tan\\theta-1)=0$.\n\nFor $\\tan\\theta=0$, the solutions are $\\theta=0^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ},\\ 360^{\\circ}$.\n\nFor $\\tan\\theta=1$, the related angle is $45^{\\circ}$ and tangent is positive in quadrants I and III, giving $\\theta=45^{\\circ},\\ 225^{\\circ}$.\n\nAll five values satisfy the original restrictions. Hence $\\theta=0^{\\circ},\\ 45^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ},\\ 225^{\\circ},\\ 360^{\\circ}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
